   "definition_quote": "Consider a MAB  with $n$ arms, each with unknown mean payoff $\\mu_1, \\dots, \\mu_n$ in $[0,1]$. A sample of the $i$th arm is an independent realization of a sub-Gaussian random variable with mean $\\mu_i$. In the \\emph{fixed confidence setting}, the goal of the best arm problem is to devise a sampling procedure with a single input $\\delta$ that ... finds the arm with the largest mean with probability at least $1-\\delta$."
  },
